---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MediaFrame from '../../components/editorial/MediaFrame.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../components/editorial/SectionLabel.astro';
import { media } from '../../data/media';
import { intelligenceAreas, trustoraPrinciples, mediaManifest } from '../../data/site';
---

<Layout title="About Trustora — EoR with Employee Intelligence" description="Trustora combines Employer of Record services with specialist employee intelligence across the EU, Australia, and USA." currentPath="/about/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="measure page-hero-grid"><div class="page-hero-copy"><SectionLabel>About Trustora</SectionLabel><h1>Employment infrastructure for intelligent work.</h1><p>Trustora combines Employer of Record services with access to specialist people in AI, ML, quantum, physics, sciences, and shipped software.</p></div><div class="page-hero-note">Strong relationships across the European Union, Australia, and the United States.</div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure about-layout"><MediaFrame src={media['camera-grip-set']} alt={mediaManifest['camera-grip-set'].alt} caption="A service relationship is still a relationship." credit={mediaManifest['camera-grip-set'].credit} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 40vw" position="50% 50%" /><div><SectionLabel>Our role</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">We hold the operating details so expert people can keep doing the work.</h2><div class="prose mt-3"><p>Global hiring asks a company to connect ambition with local reality. Our role is to coordinate the employment layer around that connection: the documents, payroll, benefits, timing, questions, and handoffs that let a company employ specialist people without asking them to carry the complexity alone.</p><p>We are not trying to make employment invisible. We are trying to make it legible enough to operate with confidence.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section blue-field"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel>Employee intelligence</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">The capability beside the contract.</h2></div><p>Our relationships connect companies with people who can contribute in deep technical and scientific domains—and who understand what it takes to ship work.</p></div><div class="expertise-grid">{intelligenceAreas.map((area) => <div class="expertise-item"><span>{area.number}</span><h3>{area.title}</h3><p>{area.body}</p></div>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-field"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel light>How we work</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">The promise is a behavior.</h2></div><p>These principles are deliberately practical. They are what integrity looks like when the question is a payroll correction, a country exception, or a first day that needs more care.</p></div><div class="principle-list">{trustoraPrinciples.map((principle) => <div class="principle-row"><span class="number">{principle.number}</span><h3>{principle.title}</h3><p>{principle.body}</p></div>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure split-argument"><h2>We would rather be useful than impressive.</h2><div class="prose"><p>That means asking for the country before promising the timeline. It means separating administration from advice. It means giving a team a responsibility map instead of a collection of confident nouns.</p><p>If an answer depends on local law, tax, immigration, or a specific working relationship, we say so and help coordinate the next right conversation.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section orange-field"><div class="measure intro-slab"><div><SectionLabel light>Work with us</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Bring the question behind the question.</h2></div><div class="intro-body"><p>Tell us what you are trying to build, where the person will work, and what feels unclear. We will start there.</p><a class="button button-light" href="/contact/">Talk to Trustora <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</Layout>
